{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>His lamp</b> — an allusion to his soul; it will be extinguished, corresponding to \"shall surely die.\"" "<b>In the pupil of darkness</b> — doubled, meaning that he shall die in darkness; or the darkness is a metaphor for troubles."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:49.851604103Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}